<title>USA: Toll Brothers adopts holder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Toll Brothers adopts holder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>HUNTINGDON VALLEY, Pa 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toll Brothers Inc said Friday its board adopted a shareholder rights plan to protect shareholders should someone try to take over the company.</p>
<p>The rights plan would take effect if someone acquires or tries to acquire 15 percent or more of the company's common stock, said company spokesman Joseph Sicree.</p>
<p>Rights will be distributed as a dividend at the rate of one right for each share of common stock held by shareholders of record July 11, 1997.</p>
<p>The Rights will expire July 11, 2007, the company said.</p>
<p>Toll Brothers Inc is a builder of luxury homes.</p>
</text>
